    "rawResponses": {
      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a bank.\n2: MATCH 11 -- Same organizational unit concept.\n3: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an IT operations team.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service desk.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network operations centre.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security operations centre.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an application owner.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a technical owner.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business owner.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business process.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service level objective.\n12: NO MATCH -- Infrastructure is broader than an infrastructure component.\n13: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a server.\n14: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a virtual machine.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a container platform.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cloud service.\n17: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network device.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network segment.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an endpoint.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a storage system.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data centre.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a site.\n23: NO MATCH -- A recovery environment is narrower than an environment.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data asset.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring tool.\n26: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring rule.\n27: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a metric.\n28: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a log source.\n29: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security event.\n30: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a major incident.\n31: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cybersecurity incident.\n32: NO MATCH -- A problem record documents a problem; it is not the problem.\n33: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an emergency change.\n34: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a release.\n35: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business continuity plan.\n36: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a disaster recovery test.",
      "relationships": "1: NO MATCH -- Routing an incident to a group is not the same as resolving it or assigning it.\n2: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes engineer membership in a resolver group.\n3: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes commander membership in the response team.\n4: MATCH 5 -- An IT service owned by a service owner is the reciprocal of the owner owning it.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes vendor support for an application.\n6: MATCH 15 -- A notification addressed to a regulator is sent to that regulator.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a stakeholder's interest in a business service.\n8: MATCH 4 -- An IT service supporting a business service expresses the reciprocal dependency.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an IT service exposing an interface.\n10: NO MATCH -- A plan applying to a service does not specify that it recovers the service.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects a recovery plan to a backup set.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects an event to the configuration item where it was observed.\n13: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects an event to an IT service.\n14: NO MATCH -- Arising from an event describes origin, not indicating the event.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects an alert to an IT service.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects an alert to a configuration item.\n17: NO MATCH -- Linking an alert to an incident does not say the alert may open it.\n18: NO MATCH -- Linking an event to an incident does not specify correlation from the event.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident's impact on a business service.\n20: NO MATCH -- Assignment to an engineer does not establish that the engineer handles the incident.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects an incident to a runbook.\n22: NO MATCH -- Preserving evidence is different from an evidence item documenting an incident.\n23: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident notifying a stakeholder.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes escalation of an incident to a vendor.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects an incident to a recovery plan.\n26: MATCH 10 -- An incident's materiality assessment is the assessment that evaluates it.\n27: MATCH 12 -- An incident having a post-incident review is reviewed in that review.\n28: MATCH 24 -- A known error documenting a workaround expresses that it has that workaround.\n29: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects a known error to an affected configuration item.\n30: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a workaround documented in a runbook.\n31: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a deployment deploying an application.\n32: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a review producing a corrective action.\n33: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a change implementing a corrective action.\n34: MATCH 11 -- An assessment leading to a notification expresses the triggering connection.\n35: MATCH 14 -- A regulatory notification for an incident reports that incident.\n36: NO MATCH -- Evidence supporting a notification need not be included in it.",
